  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduccion de la incidencia y la mortalidad por tuberculosis en la Republica Dominicana, focalizando intervenciones en poblacion clave y grupos de riesgo para el Fin de la epidemia en el pais. - Dominican Republic (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dominican Republic, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Public Health and Social Assistance of the Dominican Republic (MSP)This program has the following goals: Reduce TB incidence through a rapid increase in detection and successful treatment of cases in key populations and high-transmission urban areas with large city characteristics..  Reduce TB mortality through ensuring detection and early treatment of cases of TB/HIV co-infection and multidrug-resistant TB and/or rifampicin-resistant TB.. The objectives of this program are: Increase detection and successful treatment of MDR-TB and RR-TB through reducing the delay in diagnosis and in starting treatment..  Increase detection and successful treatment of TB cases, focusing on populations deprived of liberty and Haitian migrants, and on large cities.  Increase detection, early treatment and prevention of TB/HIV, ensuring universal access to rapid molecular tests and IPT for all PLHIV, HIV screening for TB patients, CPT and initiation of ARVs for all co-infected patients</narrative>
  </description>
